<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8">
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
        <title>Plumes</title>
        <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
        <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
        <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cinzel+Decorative:wght@400;700;900&family=Poppins:ital,wght@0,100;0,200;0,300;0,400;0,500;0,600;0,700;0,800;0,900;1,100;1,200;1,300;1,400;1,500;1,600;1,700;1,800;1,900&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
        <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cinzel+Decorative:wght@400;700;900&family=Cormorant+Garamond:ital,wght@0,300..700;1,300..700&family=Poppins:ital,wght@0,100;0,200;0,300;0,400;0,500;0,600;0,700;0,800;0,900;1,100;1,200;1,300;1,400;1,500;1,600;1,700;1,800;1,900&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.0.0/css/all.min.css">
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/styles.css">
    </head>
    <body>
        <header>
            <h2 class="logo"><i class="fa-solid fa-feather"></i> Plumes</h2>
            <nav>
                <ul class="nav-links">
                   <li><a href="/login"><i class="fa-solid fa-user"></i> Log in</a></li>
                   <li><a href="/signup"><i class="fa-solid fa-user-plus"></i> Create Account</a></li>
                   <li><a href="#"><i class="fa-solid fa-envelope"></i> Contact</a></li>
                </ul>
            </nav>
        </header>
        <main>
            <section class="intro">
                <h1>Your artistic hub,<br/> simplified.</h1>
                <img class="colors" src="/img/colors.webp" alt="paint">
            </section>
            <section>
            </section>
            <div class="quote-container">
                <div>
                    <img src="/img/tree.webp" alt="music tree">
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p class="quote">"Art is the lie that enables us to realize the truth."</p>
                    <p class="quote-author">— Pablo Picasso</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </main>
        <section class="categories">
            <section class="about">
                <div class="app-summary">
                    <p>Plumes is designed for <span>artists</span>, <span>writers</span>, and <span>creators</span> to effortlessly capture and organize their work. Whether you're crafting song lyrics, melodies, or visual inspirations, Plumes keeps everything in one place so your creativity flows without limits.</p>
                </div>
            </section>
            <div class="category-grid">
                <div class="category-item">
                    <p>Save and refine your song lyrics, whether it’s a single verse or a full composition.</p>
                    <button class="category-btn lyrics"><a href="/login">Song lyrics</a></button>
                </div>
                <div class="category-item">
                    <p>Store musical ideas, recordings, or notes for future inspiration.</p>
                    <button class="category-btn melodies"><a href="/login">Recordings</a></button>
                </div>
                <div class="category-item">
                    <p>Organize sketches, digital renderings, or artwork related to your creations.</p>
                    <button class="category-btn art"><a href="/login">Art</a></button>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div>
                <img src="/img/woman.webp">
            </div>
        </section>
        <footer>
            <div class="footer-content">
                <p>&copy; 2025 Plumes | All Rights Reserved</p>
                <nav class="footer-links">
                    <a href="#">About</a>
                    <a href="#">Privacy Policy</a>
                    <a href="#">Terms of Service</a>
                    <a href="#">Contact</a>
                </nav>
            </div>
        </footer>    
    </body>
</html>

<!-- Yes, building a basic app to store artistic ideas within 3 weeks is achievable, particularly if you focus on a simple, user-friendly design and utilize tools that streamline the development process. 
Elaboration: 
Focus on core functionality:
    -Prioritize the essential features like storing images, text notes, and perhaps a basic organization system (e.g., categories, tags). 
Utilize low-code platforms:
    -Consider platforms like Iubenda or other low-code/no-code solutions that can help automate code generation, saving development time. 
Simplify the user interface (UI):
    -A clean, intuitive interface will make the app easy to use and avoid unnecessary complexity. 
Prioritize testing:
    -Thoroughly test the app's functionality to ensure a smooth user experience. 
Consider external storage (Cloud):
    -If you want the app to be accessible across devices and without needing to copy files manually, consider using a cloud storage service like Google Drive or Dropbox. 
Iterate and refine:
    -After the initial launch, you can gather feedback from users and iterate on the design to add more features and improve the overall experience. 
Example of a simple app: 
1. Image Storage: Allow users to upload images of their artistic ideas. 
2. Text Notes: Enable users to add text descriptions or notes related to the images. 
3. Basic Organization: Introduce a simple categorization system (e.g., sketches, paintings, digital art). 
4. User Interface: Focus on ease of use with a clear and concise interface. 
5. Testing: Test all features to ensure the app works as expected.
6. Optional (Cloud Storage): Integrate with a cloud service for data persistence. -->
